  "notes": "The opposite is {値下|ねさ}がり (price decrease). A related but different term is {値上|ねあ}げ (a deliberate price hike by a seller), whereas {値上|ねあ}がり describes the price going up on its own or from external factors.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {値上|ねあ}がりが{続|つづ}く (prices continue to rise)\n- {大幅|おおはば}な{値上|ねあ}がり (significant price increase)\n- {株価|かぶか}の{値上|ねあ}がり (stock price appreciation)\n- {値上|ねあ}がりを{見込|みこ}む (expect prices to rise)",
